# CIS Critical Security Controls version 8 — 18 controls and their safeguards,
# with the three Implementation Groups as profiles.

@id cis-controls-v8
@name CIS Critical Security Controls v8
@version 8.0
@publisher Center for Internet Security
@description Prioritised safeguards for cyber defence, grouped into Implementation Groups IG1, IG2 and IG3.
@source https://www.cisecurity.org/controls

@profile ig1 = Implementation Group 1 | Essential cyber hygiene. The safeguards every enterprise should implement.
@profile ig2 = Implementation Group 2 | IG1 plus safeguards for enterprises with dedicated security staff.
@profile ig3 = Implementation Group 3 | IG2 plus safeguards for enterprises with security experts across specialities.

@family 1 = Inventory and Control of Enterprise Assets
@family 2 = Inventory and Control of Software Assets
@family 3 = Data Protection
@family 4 = Secure Configuration of Enterprise Assets and Software
@family 5 = Account Management
@family 6 = Access Control Management
@family 7 = Continuous Vulnerability Management
@family 8 = Audit Log Management
@family 9 = Email and Web Browser Protections
@family 10 = Malware Defenses
@family 11 = Data Recovery
@family 12 = Network Infrastructure Management
@family 13 = Network Monitoring and Defense
@family 14 = Security Awareness and Skills Training
@family 15 = Service Provider Management
@family 16 = Application Software Security
@family 17 = Incident Response Management
@family 18 = Penetration Testing

1.1 | Establish and Maintain Detailed Enterprise Asset Inventory | ig1,ig2,ig3
1.2 | Address Unauthorized Assets | ig1,ig2,ig3
1.3 | Utilize an Active Discovery Tool | ig2,ig3
1.4 | Use Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol (DHCP) Logging to Update Enterprise Asset Inventory | ig2,ig3
1.5 | Use a Passive Asset Discovery Tool | ig3

